From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpl: -clusters_file, groups of cells pulled toward an anchor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Nesterov placement minimises the sum of wirelength plus a density
penalty. A module whose partners sit on opposite sides of the die is
spread between them by that sum, and the paths inside it pay: on
XiangShan's XSTile parent, CtrlBlock's cells fill 8 % of their bounding
box and its worst paths are a wall of control logic at 2,406 ps, where
the same module placed alone closes at 1,200 ps.

global_placement -clusters_file <json> names groups of cells by
instance-name prefix; each group's cells are pulled toward its anchor,
or its own centroid when it has none:

  {"tau_iter": 0,
   "clusters": [{"name": "CtrlBlock",
                 "prefixes": ["core/backend/inner_ctrlBlock"],
                 "anchor_um": [1200, 1250],
                 "weight": 1.0}]}

The pull is the descent direction of k * |x - a|^2, k chosen so that a
cell one RMS radius from the centroid is pulled with `weight` times the
mean wirelength gradient. With tau_iter > 0 it decays as
exp(-iter / tau_iter): a short tau shapes the start of placement and
lets go, as DG-RePlAce's cluster constraint does (Kahng et al., IEEE
TCAD 2024); 0 holds the group to the end. The file is meant to come from
the macro placer's clustering (rtl_macro_placer), which already places
standard-cell clusters as soft macros. Hard stops: an unreadable or
malformed file (GPL-0343/0344), a group that matches no cell
(GPL-0342). CPU only: the GPU path refuses it (GPL-0340).

Not upstreamed; carried in bazel-orfs to measure on CoralNPU and
XiangShan first.
